## The Forecasting Company — t0-alpha / t0-beta

This repo is a from-scratch Rust/Burn/wgpu port of The Forecasting
Company's t0-alpha and t0-beta time-series forecasting models.

- Reference weights and code: https://huggingface.co/theforecastingcompany/t0-alpha
  and https://huggingface.co/theforecastingcompany/t0-beta
- Reference PyTorch implementation: `tfc-t0` on PyPI
  (https://pypi.org/project/tfc-t0/)
- License: Apache License, Version 2.0

No original code from `tfc-t0` is copied into this repo; the port is a
from-scratch reimplementation against the published architecture and the
reference model's numerical behavior (see `docs/reports/t0-alpha.md`).

## gluonts

`tools/score_gifteval.py` and `tools/score_official_protocol.py` compute
accuracy metrics (MASE, weighted quantile loss) using gluonts's evaluation
functions (`gluonts.ev`, `gluonts.model.evaluate_model`).

- Project: https://github.com/awslabs/gluonts
- License: Apache License, Version 2.0

## GIFT-Eval

The accuracy benchmark protocol, task configs, and dataset windowing used
by the GIFT-Eval scoring tools (`tools/gifteval_subset.py`,
`tools/gifteval_official_export.py`, `fixtures/gifteval/`) come from the
GIFT-Eval benchmark.

- Project: https://github.com/SalesforceAIResearch/gift-eval
- License: Apache License, Version 2.0
- The underlying per-dataset time series (e.g. `electricity`, `solar`,
  `jena_weather`, `saugeenday`, `LOOP_SEATTLE`, `us_births`) are drawn from
  GIFT-Eval's own dataset collection, largely sourced from the Monash Time
  Series Forecasting Archive (Godahewa et al. 2021,
  https://forecastingdata.org/) and similar public research archives.
  See GIFT-Eval's own documentation for the license of each individual
  dataset; `web/data/README.md` in this repo documents the specific
  provenance and license (CC BY 4.0 / public domain) of the one series
  bundled with the browser demo (`us_births`).

